AI RESUME SCREENER PIPELINE
(VERY CLEAR – STEP BY STEP – BEGINNER LEVEL)

============================================================
STEP 1: START PROGRAM

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - User runs app.py
    - App loads dataset file

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

DATA FILE USED:
    - data/raw/ai_resume_dataset_2025.csv

MODULE USED:
    - modules/data_loader.py

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Reads CSV file using pandas
    - Stores data inside a DataFrame
    - Sends data to next step

============================================================
STEP 2: FILTER JOB ROLE

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - User selects a job role (example: Data Scientist)
    - Program keeps only candidates for that role

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

MODULE USED:
    - modules/data_loader.py

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - df = df[df["Job Role"] == selected_role]
    - Now we only work with relevant candidates

============================================================
STEP 3: CLEAN THE DATA

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - Convert skills to lowercase
    - Remove extra spaces
    - Split skills by comma
    - Convert Experience to number
    - Convert Projects Count to number
    - Replace missing Certifications with empty

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

MODULE USED:
    - modules/preprocessing.py

OUTPUT FILE CREATED:
    - data/processed/cleaned_resume_data.csv

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Makes data clean
    - Removes errors
    - Makes it ready for ML

============================================================
STEP 4: CONVERT TEXT TO NUMBERS (FEATURE ENGINEERING)

WHY:
    - Machine learning cannot understand text
    - We must convert text into numbers

WHAT HAPPENS:

PART A – SKILLS
    - Apply TF-IDF on Skills column
    - Convert skill text into numeric vectors

PART B – EDUCATION
    - Convert education to score
        PhD = 4
        MBA = 3
        B.Sc = 2
        Others = 1

PART C – EXPERIENCE
    - Normalize experience (scale 0–1)

PART D – PROJECTS
    - Normalize projects count

PART E – CERTIFICATION
    - If certification exists → 1
    - If none → 0

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

MODULE USED:
    - modules/feature_engineering.py

MODEL SAVED:
    - models/tfidf_vectorizer.pkl

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Converts all resume features into numbers

============================================================
STEP 5: SKILL MATCH CALCULATION

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - Convert job role text into TF-IDF vector
    - Compare candidate skills with job role
    - Use Cosine Similarity

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

MODULE USED:
    - modules/similarity.py

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Calculates skill similarity score (0 to 1)
    - Example:
        0.85 means 85% skill match

============================================================
STEP 6: CALCULATE FINAL SCORE

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - Combine all scores:

        Skill Score
        Experience Score
        Education Score
        Projects Score
        Certification Score

    - Apply weights:
        Skills = 40%
        Experience = 20%
        Education = 15%
        Projects = 15%
        Certification = 10%

    - Final Score = Combined weighted score
    - Convert to 0–100 scale

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

MODULE USED:
    - modules/scoring.py
    - utils/helper.py

OUTPUT FILE CREATED:
    - outputs/final_scores.csv

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Creates one final performance score

============================================================
STEP 7: RANK CANDIDATES

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - Sort candidates by Final Score (highest first)
    - Assign Rank

        Highest score = Rank 1
        Second highest = Rank 2

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

MODULE USED:
    - modules/ranking.py

OUTPUT FILE CREATED:
    - outputs/ranked_candidates.csv

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Creates final ranking list

============================================================
STEP 8: DISPLAY RESULTS

WHAT HAPPENS:
    - Show:
        Name
        Skills
        Experience
        Final Score
        Rank
        Original AI Score (for comparison)

    - Allow user to download CSV

MAIN FILE:
    - app.py

FILES USED:
    - outputs/ranked_candidates.csv
    - outputs/final_scores.csv

WHAT THIS STEP DOES:
    - Shows final output to recruiter

